From a48f3b150a795fa22c5fbc071d7b6d6043c72591 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:33:11 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 38/60] Muse Spark Open on CUDA: config, EXL3 pack loader,
 decode forward (one GPU)

families/muse_spark: Config.parse (text_config of muse_spark; refuses dense MLPs, shared experts, attention
bias, tied embeddings, head_dim != 64, GQA != 8, non-default RoPE), rank cuts for TP=2 (q / gate / o by heads,
k / v by KV heads, pre / post expert projections by latent halves, experts by width, head on 128-row blocks:
790 + 789), the loader (MiMo-V2's EXL3 pack helpers; norm weights as 1 + w, residual gates as alpha / beta,
the fp32 router stored as bf16 when exact), and the decode forward for windows of rows over any slots:
embedding norm, centred RMS norms, weightless QK norm + NeoX RoPE (NoPE on full layers), head_dim 64 decode
attention (hand CUDA: a block per row / KV head / 256-key chunk, eight query heads as warps over shared
K / V tiles), o_norm and the sigmoid output gate, learned residual gates with the post norms, fp32
sigmoid + bias top-8 router, latent MoE (pre_expert_proj + centred norm, MiMo-V2's EXL3 grouped experts,
per-expert input-scaled norm before the routing weight), post_expert_proj, the softcapped head.
tf-muse m1 runs it teacher-forced against exllamav3's answer key (tools/g5 in the Muse recipe).
TP=2, graphs and the lanes backend are not wired yet (Model.init refuses world > 1).
